cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository in your research, please cite the associated
  manuscript listed under preferred-citation. The manuscript has been submitted
  for peer review and is not yet published.

title: "TR-TRP: Tower Repositioning and Technician Routing Problem for Communication Recovery"
type: software

# Replace the placeholder author information below with the repository authors.
authors:
  - family-names: "YOUR_FAMILY_NAME"
    given-names: "YOUR_GIVEN_NAMES"

abstract: >-
  Research code, computational instances, configuration files, and numerical
  results for the Tower Repositioning and Technician Routing Problem for
  Communication Recovery (TR-TRP). The project studies the coordinated
  deployment of mobile communication towers and technician crews following a
  disruption, including deterministic and robust variants.

keywords:
  - "tower repositioning"
  - "technician routing"
  - "communication recovery"
  - "robust optimization"
  - "routing"
  - "disaster recovery"

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The Tower Repositioning and Technician Routing Problem for Communication Recovery"
  status: submitted

  # Replace the placeholder author information below with the manuscript authors,
  # in the same order used in the submitted paper.
  authors:
    - family-names: "YOUR_FAMILY_NAME"
      given-names: "YOUR_GIVEN_NAMES"
